The latest MSTest is **4.2.3**. Here are the breaking changes that **directly affect your project**:

---

## 1. `[ExpectedException]` is removed (CRITICAL)

Your two tests use `[ExpectedException(...)]`, which no longer exists in v4. Replace with `Assert.ThrowsExactly<T>`:

```csharp
// Before
[ExpectedException(typeof(ArgumentNullException))]
[TestMethod]
public void Validate_NullInput_ThrowsArgumentNull()
{
    Validate(null);
}

// After
[TestMethod]
public void Validate_NullInput_ThrowsArgumentNull()
{
    Assert.ThrowsExactly<ArgumentNullException>(() => Validate(null));
}
```

Do the same for `Process_InvalidState_ThrowsInvalidOperation`.

## 2. `Assert.IsTrue(true)` triggers warning MSTEST0032

Your `Validate_ValidInput_Succeeds` test has `Assert.IsTrue(true)` which is flagged as always-true. Replace with a meaningful assertion or suppress.

## 3. Other notable v4 changes (less likely to affect you)

| Change | Impact |
|--------|--------|
| `TestMethodAttribute.Execute` → `ExecuteAsync` | Only if you have custom test method attributes |
| `ClassCleanupBehavior` enum removed | Only if you use `ClassCleanup(ClassCleanupBehavior.EndOfClass)` |
| `Assert` APIs no longer accept `message + object[]` params | Use string interpolation instead |
| Minimum TFM is net8.0 | You're already on net8.0 ✅ |
| Analyzer severities upgraded to Warning | May cause new warnings in CI with `-TreatWarningsAsErrors` |

---

Would you like me to upgrade the project and fix the tests?
